From 105ae02004f3beeb087cdf832cf1297d476fee92 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 09:40:52 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 6/8] Fix vessel fixture mapping, UTC timestamps, fps display;
 lean score history

Frontend
- V2-only fixtures (sensors, access log, cyber findings) are attached to
  backend vessels by a stable slot (vessels sorted by ID) instead of the API
  list position, and only vessel identity/score fields are taken from the
  backend (no stray "score"/"state" keys on Vessel).
- Timestamps without an offset (SQLite) are parsed as UTC. Browsers treated
  them as local time, so in Tallinn (UTC+3) every event/incident time was
  shifted by three hours.
- Camera fps no longer shows "24.900000000000006".

Backend
- Score history is appended only when a vessel's score changes, and the
  previous score is read with a single LIMIT 1 query instead of loading the
  whole history for every vessel on every simulation step.

Tests: tests/test_score_history.py.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
